// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Reflection-probes manual test map. Covers the Manual rows of
// context/plans/in-progress/reflection-probes/index.md.
// Axis-aligned box brushes; 1 map unit = 0.0254 m; map coordinates, Z up.
// Keep comments free of braces and quotes and
// never leave a blank line inside an entity block. A bare comment marker with
// no text after it also breaks the parser.
// Fluid water is declared in content/dev/start-script.ts.
// Script: content/dev/scripts/reflection-probes-test.ts.
// ----
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/reflection-probes-test.map -o content/dev/maps/reflection-probes-test.prl
// Run:     cargo run -p xtask -- run --features dev-tools -- content/dev/maps/reflection-probes-test.prl
// ----
// LAYOUT, west to east along X, every room y 0 to 512:
//   Room P, pool room     x 0 to 512,     floor z 0, ceiling z 256, grey concrete walls
//   Door P to A           x 512 to 528,   y 400 to 464, onto room A north walkway
//   Room A, canal west    x 528 to 912,   floor z 0, ceiling z 192, RED walls
//   Doorway A to B        x 912 to 928,   y 144 to 368, z 0 to 128, the canal runs under it
//   Room B, canal hall    x 928 to 1440,  floor z 0, ceiling z 384, GREEN walls
//   Balcony               x 1312 to 1440, top z 192, stairs along the south wall x 1024 to 1312
// ----
// POOL ROOM P
//   Pool        x 160 to 352, y 160 to 352, surface z 0 flush with the floor, pit floor z -96 blue.
//   Coping      16 wide, 6 high, x 144 to 368, y 144 to 368.
//   Floor props crate x 392 to 440, y 200 to 248, 48 high, east of the rim;
//               bench x 200 to 312, y 104 to 128, 20 high, south of the rim;
//               stump x 88 to 120, y 88 to 120, 64 high, in the sdf corner.
//   Neon sign   x 192 to 320 on the north wall y 512, z 96 to 160, faces the pool.
//   Lights      static fill 256 384 224;
//               FLICKER, Quake style 10, amber, 96 400 208, north-west of the pool;
//               SWITCHABLE, cyan, tag rp_switch_light, 432 128 208, south-east;
//               SDF, _shadow_type sdf, magenta, 40 40 160, south-west corner.
//   Switches    on the south wall: red x 352 to 384 turns the tagged lights OFF,
//               green x 448 to 480 turns them back ON. Walk up, press use.
//   Start       256 56, facing north across the pool at the neon sign.
// ----
// CANAL, one fluid_volume, surface z -16, through rooms A and B:
//   Room A stretch x 528 to 920, y 208 to 304: DERIVED probe, red walls.
//   Room B stretch x 920 to 1440, y 208 to 304, widened to a basin y 112 to 400
//   from x 928: claimed by the AUTHORED reflection_volume x 928 to 1440, y 0 to
//   512, z -96 to 384, _capture_offset -128 0. A pillar x 1168 to 1200,
//   y 240 to 272 stands at the basin centroid; the offset moves the capture
//   point west, clear of it. The brush split at x 920 is the doorway midline.
//   Room B has a second SWITCHABLE cyan light, same tag, at 1200 440 300, and a
//   red OFF and green ON switch pair on the east wall above the balcony.
// ----
// WHAT TO LOOK FOR, per Manual row
//   Row 37, existing map: not this map; rebuild e24-environment-test.map.
//   Row 38, mirror: from the start, the pool mirrors the room, the magenta sdf
//     corner and the stump shadow included. Strafe along y 56: the north wall
//     and neon sign hold their place. Crouch or stand on the coping edge for a
//     low eye: coping, crate, bench and stump reflect at the right height.
//   Row 39, Fresnel: look straight down from the coping, faint; look across the
//     pool, near-mirror. Climb the stairs to the balcony and look west across
//     the basin and canal: far walls and the green ceiling reflect strongly.
//   Row 40, live light: watch the amber flicker in the pool reflection, no seam
//     between lobes. Press the red pool-room switch: the south-east cyan wash
//     leaves the reflection there; green restores it. Repeat from the balcony
//     with its own switches and watch the basin. The neon sign reflects.
//   Row 41, pixel style: per the manifest water fluid reflection style.
//   Row 42, canal boundary: stand in room A or on the balcony looking along the
//     canal through the doorway. Where the derived room A probe meets the
//     authored room B probe at x 920, expect at most a brightness or occlusion
//     step, never a geometry jump.
{
"classname" "worldspawn"
"wad" ""
"data_script" "../scripts/reflection-probes-test.ts"
"_tb_mod" "dev"
"_tb_def" "external:../../../sdk/TrenchBroom/postretro.fgd"
